>> title: Pork Chop Bun
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: pork, sandwich, roll, macau, hong kong, stovetop
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: jyu paa baau, 豬扒包, pork chop bun, Macau pork chop bun, Macanese pork bun, Portuguese pork bun
>> servings: 2
>> time: 40 min

>> step: pound thin, marinate, rest 30 min
Pound @bone-in pork chops{2}(6 oz each; to 1/2 in) and rub them with @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @Shaoxing wine{2%tsp}, @sugar{1%tsp}, @white pepper{1/2%tsp}, @five-spice powder{1/4%tsp}, @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and @cornstarch{2%tsp}, then ~rest{30%min}.

>> step: fry 6 min, both sides, edges crisp
Fry @&(~1)pork chops{} in @neutral oil{1%Tbs} in a #frying pan{} for ~fry{6%min}, turning once, until the edges have crisped.

>> step: warm 3 min and split them
Warm @crusty white rolls{2}(a bolillo or Portuguese roll is closest; a soft bun is not) in a hot #oven{} for ~warm{3%min}, then split them and butter the cut faces with @salted butter{2%tsp}.

>> step: press the lid down — nothing else goes in
Lay @&(~2)pork chop{} into @&(~1)roll{} with the bone still in it and press the lid down.
